        <mxCell id="n-RRbNjujNcNdDWotRqD-1" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="34.98" width="173.5" x="976" y="26.50999999999999" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n-RRbNjujNcNdDWotRqD-2" parent="1" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=data:image/png,;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="48" width="48" x="20" y="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="KAmA-6OsdgUMxD263_WL-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;autosize=1;resizable=0;" value="&lt;h1&gt;Detailed wiring of SBUS interface for receiver RC and LCD&lt;/h1&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="690" x="225" y="53" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="iPKEfCxZtc5BU-QmLC5g-1" parent="1" style="shape=note;size=20;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=center;perimeterSpacing=3;spacingLeft=11;spacingRight=16;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;SBUS requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;362&quot; data-end=&quot;380&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;inverted logic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;. However, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;395&quot; data-end=&quot;456&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Arduino Mega cannot directly handle inverted SBUS signals&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;, therefore an&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;471&quot; data-end=&quot;493&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;IC 74HC14 inverter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;is used to convert the signal before it is read by the Arduino&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;2. V&lt;/span&gt;oltage drop issue on the main PCB make the Arduino &lt;b&gt;only receives around 4.1V&lt;/b&gt; as its supply voltage&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;If additional components also take power from the PCB or the Arduino 5V pin, the voltage drop problem may become worse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;741&quot; data-end=&quot;857&quot;&gt;To solve this issue, additional components &lt;b&gt;should take the 5V supply directly from the TDK-Lambda step-down converte&lt;/b&gt;r. This method helps prevent additional load on the main PCB power line&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;741&quot; data-end=&quot;857&quot;&gt;3. Separated&lt;strong data-start=&quot;900&quot; data-end=&quot;928&quot; style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;ground connection&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;is very important in this wiring system&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;741&quot; data-end=&quot;857&quot;&gt;The ground from the battery, called “GND1”, contains a lot of electrical noise. Currently, the battery ground and the PCB ground are separated (isolated). &lt;b&gt;Therefore, GND1 and the PCB ground should never be connected together,&lt;/b&gt; because the motor noise can make the system unstable&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="440" width="280" x="40" y="350" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="iKXJDGe19YCRODIGM-6u-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="iKXJDGe19YCRODIGM-6u-1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeColor=#FF0000;strokeWidth=2;" target="mz5oU6mLIlolYrWPV2eN-6">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1110" y="238" />
              <mxPoint x="1110" y="470" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="9J9RQpMdP2JIoG6TYy8P-2" edge="1" parent="1" source="9J9RQpMdP2JIoG6TYy8P-1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;strokeWidth=2;" target="mz5oU6mLIlolYrWPV2eN-7">
